d\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87PBfr_\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"LengUNC\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"NONE\",\n      \"body\": \"I apologize for the inconvenience. Please remove \\\"multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions\\\" from the terms definitions as we are still evaluating the gene-disease association. Please use the revised definitions as below.\\n\\nNew term description for SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder:\\nA heterogeneous collection of cardiac rhythm disorders caused by genetic variation in the SCN5A gene with autosomal dominant inheritance. Affected individuals are commonly reported to have unremarkable cardiac morphology and at least one cardiac rhythm phenotype that includes, but is not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, long QT syndrome, and Brugada syndrome. Individuals with pathogenic variants in SCN5A may also exhibit overlapping or mixed cardiac rhythm phenotypes and intrafamilial variability.\\n\\nNew term description for Cardiogenetic rhythm disorders: \\nA heterogeneous group of cardiac rhythm phenotypes with a monogenic etiology that include, but are not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, Brugada syndrome, long QT syndrome, short QT syndrome, tachycardia with fibrillation, etc.\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-10-31T14:12:09Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"THUMBS_UP\",\n          \"users\": {\n            \"totalCount\": 1\n          }","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778614100700,"end":1778614100706}},"id":"prt_e1da961c2001UNg3OHHmbnbCOr","sessionID":"ses_1e2573d8effehHK6MzSMzsUiGg","messageID":"msg_e1da952790014IDkRluKyYXayR"}}
