{"type":"text","timestamp":1778615334341,"sessionID":"ses_1e2573d8effehHK6MzSMzsUiGg","part":{"id":"prt_e1dbbf668001ApQB8FDHYLjwp2","messageID":"msg_e1dbbba04001FzdFS3fcI15RAp","sessionID":"ses_1e2573d8effehHK6MzSMzsUiGg","type":"text","text":"All changes for issue #9707 have been completed and committed locally.\n\n**Summary of what was done:**\n\n1. Created **MONDO:7770003 - cardiogenetic rhythm disorder** as a new grouping term under `cardiac rhythm disease` and `cardiogenetic disease`.\n\n2. Created **MONDO:7770004 - SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder** as a new term under `cardiogenetic rhythm disorder`, `cardiac rhythm disease`, and `cardiogenetic disease`, with a logical definition following the gene-disease pattern.\n\n3. Reorganized existing terms:\n   - The five SCN5A-specific phenotypes were added as children of `MONDO:7770004`\n   - Eight monogenic cardiac rhythm disorder categories were added as children of `MONDO:7770003`\n   - Atrioventricular block was explicitly excluded per @katiermullen's comment\n\n4. Quality control performed:\n   - OBO syntax validated with `robot convert`\n   - File normalized with `make NORM`\n   - Logical consistency checked with `robot reason` (no unsatisfiable classes found)\n\n**Files created (not committed):**\n- `ISSUE_COMMENTS.md` - status update for the GitHub issue\n- `PR_COMMENTS.md` - detailed description of the changes and rationale\n\nYou can review the commit and the two markdown files before any push is performed.","time":{"start":1778615318120,"end":1778615334339}}}
